summary: a Linux program linked with --link=libc, where compiler.c_runtime is true, looks root and group zero up by ID and by name through the C library and NSS rather than reading /etc/passwd and /etc/group itself, finds the process's own account by name when it has one, and refuses an ID and a name no database holds, a name holding a colon and a buffer too small with ERANGE, as runtime/posix-accounts does on a static one
